buildings about 2,000 more or less in the past 20 years well what do you

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:15.110
want to show me first on our architectural tour maybe we started over

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:20.880
at the Pete's Hot House on Bayou St. John the Bayou was the old Indian portage

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.510
that they took to get from the Lake Pontchartrain area to the Highland of

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:27.690
the Mississippi River and in many ways it's where the history of the city began

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.030
So this is the Bayou?

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:38.200
The Bayou St. John connects the lake this way and the river on this side over here.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.280
So it runs into the river?

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:41.080
Not quite. It came very close, though.

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.240
What about the house itself?

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:49.330
Pete's Hot House is a great example of a West Indian-style Creole plantation house

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:54.900
and very much noted for the huge wraparound gallery or porch.

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:59.870
And that kept the sun off of the house in the hot summer months and makes it more comfortable.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.890
What do they grow here?

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:06.460
Indigo was the first major agricultural product, and then eventually sugar cane.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:08.570
Is indigo the coloring agent?

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:10.150
Right, like the shutters on my house.

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:11.040
Of course.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.400
I do love the columns.

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:15.170
What's the building made up?

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:22.000
The building is, first floor is solid brick, masonry construction, and then the second floor is heavy timbered.

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:29.780
It's called brick entrepoteaux, and it's actually soft bricks infilled between heavy timber construction.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.360
And it's always protected because the bricks are not very strong.

00:22:33.590 --> 00:22:34.150
And they'll melt.

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:36.150
They'll melt, right, and thicken this rain.

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:40.650
And then the roof is typical of the West Indies-style roofs, the double-pitch.

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:43.330
Again, there's a huge truss in the attic, very heavy-duty.

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:45.860
